# Frost Bay external cooler (CoolingSystem_ONEC1) — ignore its phantom HID input.
#
# The cooler advertises a HID-over-GATT service (0x1812) alongside its custom
# 0xFFE0/0xFFE1 control service, and pairs like a normal HID device. Whenever
# it is connected, bluetoothd attaches the HOG input profile and creates a
# uhid input device named after the peripheral. The cooler's ~1 Hz telemetry
# notifications are then fed to the kernel HID parser, whose consumer-control
# mapping injects Volume-Down key events — dropping system volume one step per
# second for as long as the device stays connected (the connection is owned by
# bluetoothd, not by xmaxd).
#
# The input device is useless to userspace: all cooler telemetry and control
# flows through xmaxd over GATT (0xFFE1). Tell libinput — and thus GNOME/mutter
# and anything else using libinput — to ignore it.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{name}=="CoolingSystem_ONEC1", ENV{LIBINPUT_IGNORE_DEVICE}="1"
